# Typography Component Usage

## Overview
DECM uses a centralized Typography component for all text rendering to ensure consistency, accessibility, and maintainability across the application.

## Component Location
[apps/web/src/components/typography/typography.tsx](mdc:apps/web/src/components/typography/typography.tsx)

## Import Statement
```tsx
import { Typography } from '@/components/typography/typography';
```

## Basic Usage

### Syntax
```tsx
<Typography variant="variant" tag="htmlTag" color="colorVariant" className="classes">
    Content
</Typography>
```

### Available Variants
- `header` - For headings and titles
- `text` - For body text and paragraphs
- (Check the component file for complete list)

### Available Color Variants
**IMPORTANT**: Always use the `color` prop instead of text color classes in `className`.
- `foreground` - Primary text color
- `foreground-alt` - Alternative foreground color
- `background` - Background color
- `background-alt` - Alternative background color
- `primary` - Brand primary color
- `secondary` - Brand secondary color
- `muted` - Muted text color
- `muted-foreground` - Muted foreground color
- `destructive` - Error/destructive text color

### Available HTML Tags
- `h1`, `h2`, `h3`, `h4`, `h5`, `h6` - Heading tags
- `p` - Paragraph
- `span` - Inline text
- `div` - Block container
- `label` - Form labels

## Usage Examples

### Headers and Titles
```tsx
// Page title with primary color
<Typography variant="header" tag="h1" color="primary" className="text-2xl font-bold">
    {t('home.hero.title')}
</Typography>

// Section heading
<Typography variant="header" tag="h2" color="foreground" className="text-xl">
    {t('features.title')}
</Typography>

// Subsection heading
<Typography variant="header" tag="h3" color="foreground" className="text-lg font-semibold">
    {t('auth.signIn')}
</Typography>
```

### Body Text
```tsx
// Paragraph text with muted color
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="muted-foreground" className="text-base">
    {t('home.hero.subtitle')}
</Typography>

// Inline text with alternative foreground
<Typography variant="text" tag="span" color="foreground-alt" className="text-sm">
    {t('common.loading')}
</Typography>
```

### Interactive Text
```tsx
// Button text
<button className="btn-primary">
    <Typography variant="text" tag="span" color="foreground-alt" className="font-medium">
        {t('auth.signUp')}
    </Typography>
</button>

// Link text
<Link to="/signup">
    <Typography variant="text" tag="span" color="foreground-alt" className="underline">
        {t('auth.hasAccount')}
    </Typography>
</Link>
```

### Lists and Navigation
```tsx
// List item
<li>
    <Typography variant="text" tag="span" color="muted-foreground">
        {t('nav.home')}
    </Typography>
</li>

// Navigation link
<Typography variant="text" tag="span" color="foreground" className="cursor-pointer">
    {t('nav.events')}
</Typography>
```

## Integration with i18n

Always combine Typography with i18n translations:

```tsx
import { Typography } from '@/components/typography/typography';
import { useTranslation } from 'react-i18next';

export const MyComponent = () => {
    const { t } = useTranslation();
    
    return (
        <div>
            <Typography variant="header" tag="h1" color="primary">
                {t('page.title')}
            </Typography>
            <Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="foreground-alt">
                {t('page.description')}
            </Typography>
        </div>
    );
};
```

