## Responsive Typography

Use Tailwind's responsive prefixes for different screen sizes:

```tsx
<Typography
    variant="header"
    tag="h1"
    color="primary"
    className="text-2xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl"
>
    {t('home.hero.title')}
</Typography>

<Typography
    variant="text"
    tag="p"
    color="foreground-alt"
    className="text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg"
>
    {t('home.hero.subtitle')}
</Typography>
```

## Styling Guidelines

### Text Colors
**CRITICAL**: Always use the `color` prop instead of text color classes in `className`.

```tsx
// ✅ Correct - Use color prop
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="foreground-alt">
    {t('text')}
</Typography>

// ❌ Wrong - Don't use text color in className
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" className="text-foreground-alt">
    {t('text')}
</Typography>
```

Available color variants:
- `foreground` - Primary text color
- `foreground-alt` - Alternative foreground color
- `muted-foreground` - Secondary text color
- `primary` - Brand color text
- `secondary` - Secondary brand color
- `background` - Background color
- `background-alt` - Alternative background color
- `muted` - Muted text color
- `destructive` - Error/destructive text color

### Font Weights
- `font-normal` - Regular text
- `font-medium` - Medium emphasis
- `font-semibold` - Important text
- `font-bold` - Headings

### Text Alignment
- `text-left` - Left aligned (default)
- `text-center` - Centered
- `text-right` - Right aligned
- `text-justify` - Justified

### Special Effects
```tsx
// Text shadow
className="[text-shadow:rgba(255,255,255,0.2)_0px_0px_4px]"

// Truncate
className="truncate"

// Line clamp
className="line-clamp-2"
```

## Best Practices

### ✅ DO:
- Always use Typography component for text
- Combine with i18n translations
- Use semantic HTML tags (`h1`, `h2`, `p`)
- **Use `color` prop for text colors**
- Add appropriate className for styling (excluding colors)
- Use responsive classes for mobile/desktop

### ❌ DON'T:
- Use plain HTML tags (`<h1>`, `<p>`) directly
- Hard-code text strings
- Mix Typography with other text components
- Skip the `tag` prop
- **Use text color classes in `className` (use `color` prop instead)**
- Use inline styles instead of Tailwind classes
- Use non-semantic tags unnecessarily

## Accessibility Considerations

```tsx
// Good: Proper heading hierarchy with color props
<Typography variant="header" tag="h1" color="primary">Main Title</Typography>
<Typography variant="header" tag="h2" color="foreground">Section</Typography>
<Typography variant="header" tag="h3" color="foreground">Subsection</Typography>

// Good: Descriptive labels with color prop
<Typography variant="text" tag="label" color="foreground" htmlFor="email">
    {t('auth.email')}
</Typography>

// Good: Sufficient color contrast using color prop
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="foreground">
    {t('content')}
</Typography>
```

