## Common Mistakes to Avoid

```tsx
// ❌ Bad: Direct HTML
<h1>My Title</h1>
<p>My text</p>

// ✅ Good: Typography component with color prop
<Typography variant="header" tag="h1" color="primary">{t('title')}</Typography>
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="foreground-alt">{t('text')}</Typography>

// ❌ Bad: Hard-coded text
<Typography variant="text" tag="p">Welcome to DECM</Typography>

// ✅ Good: i18n translation with color prop
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="foreground">{t('common.welcome')}</Typography>

// ❌ Bad: Missing tag prop
<Typography variant="text">Content</Typography>

// ✅ Good: Explicit tag and color prop
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="foreground">Content</Typography>

// ❌ Bad: Using text color in className
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" className="text-primary">{t('text')}</Typography>

// ✅ Good: Using color prop instead
<Typography variant="text" tag="p" color="primary">{t('text')}</Typography>
```

## Performance Tips

- Typography is a lightweight component, no performance concerns
- Combine with React.memo() for frequently re-rendered components
- Use proper semantic tags for better SEO and accessibility

